    {
      "@id": "skills/conduct/conduct-core/interaction-modality.md#provenance-1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Asking the person — the canonical rule (STRICT, read this first)",
      "prov:value": "**Why both, and why the chat copy comes first.** Once answered, a card shows\nonly the option that was chosen, and a dismissed card shows nothing. The chat\ntext is the only record of what was asked. Owner, 2026-09-29: *\"always put q\nin chat and structured\"*. Owner, 2026-10-23, after a Decision card arrived with\nno question or context before it: *\"i can't see what the options were, nor\nwhat the FULL context of the question. this is PROCESS FAILURE.\"*",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-29",
        "2026-10-23",
        "owner"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-29",
        "2026-10-23"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/conduct/conduct-core/interaction-modality.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "3.1 Who is typing, outside GitHub too",
      "prov:value": "An entry is keyed by a handle, and the session has to work out whose handle\nit is before the entry can apply. Owner, 2026-10-10 (bean `f1e1`): *identity\nis (provider, handle), GitHub first*. One resolver answers for every host:\n`bun run cat auth:login --all` (`cat-harness-tools/src/core/identity.ts`).\nIt prints every identity the session can see, each bare and as\n`provider:handle`:\n\n| provider | read from | vouched for by |\n|---|---|---|\n| `github` | the auth Tool's own resolver: a token, or `GITHUB_ACTOR` in Actions | GitHub |\n| `gitlab` | `GITLAB_USER_LOGIN`, only inside GitLab CI | GitLab |\n| `claude` | the agent host's signed-in account | the agent host |\n| any | `CAT_HARNESS_PERSON`, `provider:handle[,…]`, for this session only | nobody: the person says so |\n| any | the user-level store's `identities`, and the chosen entry of its `profiles` | nobody: the person says so |\n| `git` | `git config user.email`, then `user.name` | nobody: self-asserted |",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean f1e1",
        "2026-10-10",
        "owner"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/conduct/conduct-core/interaction-modality.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "4.1 Context before the question (STRICT)",
      "prov:value": "**And when a link IS the right thing — a rendered page the reader has to see\nfor themselves — it points at the page, not at the site it is on.** Owner,\n2026-09-21, after three turns of being handed a staging root while being asked\nabout one page on it: *\"next time give appropraite link\n…/branches/<branch>/<iris-replica>/\"*. Linking the root hands the reader a route the\nagent already knew, and hands it to somebody who types with difficulty. The rule\nand where the page list comes from:\n[`staging-review`](../../../sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/staging-review.md) §\"The deep-link rule\"; the failure it also\nhides: [`continual-progress`](../../../sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/continual-progress.md) §\"Link the PAGE, never the\nsite root\".",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-21",
        "owner"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-21"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/conduct/conduct-core/interaction-modality.md#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "The prose does not travel — the question object must stand alone (STRICT)",
      "prov:value": "**Measured here, 2026-09-22.** Two of four consolidation streams blocked on an\n`AskUserQuestion` and both containers then disconnected. Their reasoning was in\ntheir own transcripts. A sibling session relaying the block to the owner had to\n**reconstruct** the context from session metadata, PR bodies and bean files —\nand the owner read *the relay's* reconstruction rather than the asker's. The\naskers had done the analysis; none of it travelled. One of the four questions\nwould have committed to a different repository, so the reconstruction was\nload-bearing.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-22",
        "owner"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-22"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/conduct/conduct-core/interaction-modality.md#provenance-5",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "The question goes in the chat too — both, every time (STRICT)",
      "prov:value": "**Owner, 2026-09-29**, after a selection box was dismissed by accident:\n*\"reask question... dismall accidental. always put q in chat and structured\"*.\nThe question had been asked in the selection tool only. Dismissing the box\nclosed it, and nothing in the chat still said what was being asked, so the\ndecision vanished with one stray tap. For a person with limited hand function\na stray tap is the ordinary case, not the edge case.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-29",
        "owner"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-29"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/conduct/conduct-core/interaction-modality.md#provenance-6",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "The question goes in the chat too — both, every time (STRICT)",
      "prov:value": "And when you are the one **relaying** somebody else's blocked question: say\nthat you are relaying, and say where the answer has to be given. An answer\ntyped at the relay does not reach the asker. The reverse direction, a\nsibling getting its question to the agent that is talking with the person, and\nthe answer back, is [`hand-back-to-discussion`](hand-back-to-discussion.md)\n(owner, 2026-10-31: *\"sublings not raising cards to main\"*).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-31",
        "owner"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-31"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/conduct/conduct-core/interaction-modality.md#provenance-7",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "issue",
      "cat-harness:section": "Worked example — a real failure, 2026-09-18",
      "prov:value": "#### Worked example — a real failure, 2026-09-18\n\nEnding a turn, this agent wrote:\n\n> **next** `x4mt` — Cross-agent skill install + `fa-` prefix (#247). Unstarted,\n> and I'd want your call on prefix-at-rest vs prefix-at-install before writing\n> anything.\n\nEvery content word in the actual question is undefined. \"prefix-at-rest\" and\n\"prefix-at-install\" are terms the agent had coined *in the issue*, so answering\nmeant opening #247 and reading it — which the author had to do, and which is a\nreal cost for somebody who types with difficulty. It also states no cost for\neither option and gives no recommendation, so even after reading the issue there\nis nothing to choose between except two phrases.\n\nThe same decision, askable:\n\n> **Next up is #247** — installing this platform's skills into whichever agent\n> is running (Claude Code, Gemini CLI, Cursor), so each one can actually load\n> them. Skills would get an `fa-` prefix so their names cannot collide with the\n> host agent's own commands: `/fa-beans-tui` rather than `/beans-tui`.\n>\n> One decision shapes everything else — **where the prefix gets applied:**\n>\n> 1. **When a skill is installed into an agent** *(recommended)* — files in this\n>    repo keep their plain names, and the prefix is added as they are emitted.\n>    Nothing here has to change, and the collision is solved where collisions\n>    actually happen.\n> 2. **In this repository itself** — rename every skill file. That touches the\n>    package manifests, every `<bootstrap.processes:skill ref>` in the BPMN diagrams, two doc\n>    generators and every cross-reference between skill bodies. It is the kind\n>    of change that is painful to reverse.\n>\n> Say nothing and I will take (1) when I start.\n\nSame information, same length, and the second can be answered by typing one\ncharacter.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#247",
        "2026-09-18"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-18"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/conduct/conduct-core/interaction-modality.md#provenance-8",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "A pending question is not a STATUS — ask it (STRICT)",
      "prov:value": "Owner, 2026-09-22, after four sessions sat blocked while this agent reported\nthat they were blocked: *\"show the questions!!!!!!!! why are you not. dont say\na unansnwered question is a blocker, ask a question.\"*",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-22",
        "owner"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-22"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/conduct/conduct-core/interaction-modality.md#provenance-9",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "More than one decision pending — ask ONE, count the rest",
      "prov:value": "The six parts above are per decision, and nothing said what to do when three are\nopen at once. Stating all three in full is a wall; naming all three compactly is\nthe teaser the rule forbids. Neither is the answer."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/conduct/conduct-core/interaction-modality.md#provenance-10",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Enforced, not remembered — the layers",
      "prov:value": "This section was STRICT and complete on 2026-09-20, and was broken the same day\nby the agent implementing its neighbours. The owner: *\"ask specific questiosn w/\ncontext/ recommendations/pros/cons (see skills, why not invoked?)\"* — and the\n\"why not\" is mechanical rather than a lapse of care. The rule lives here, in the\nknowledge graph; `AGENTS.md` carries a **summary** of it; the summary omits the\nclause that was broken (the comparison goes in the prose, not in the selection\ntool's labels); and nothing sat between the agent and the question tool.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-20",
        "owner"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/conduct/conduct-core/interaction-modality.md#provenance-11",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Enforced, not remembered — the layers",
      "prov:value": "**The fourth layer was added 2026-09-26, after the owner named this failure a\nSECOND time in one session** — *\"you have yet again provided unanswered\nquestions as blockers but have not provided exactly what the questions are pros\ncons recommendations and down steam impact\"*. Nothing in this section was\nmissing: part 3 already required `downstream`, §\"More than one decision pending\"\nalready forbade the list of names, and the no-exemption clause was already\nthere.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-26",
        "owner"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-26"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/conduct/conduct-core/interaction-modality.md#provenance-12",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Enforced, not remembered — the layers",
      "prov:value": "Its fixtures are **real turns from that session** rather than invented strings,\nfor the reason bean `yx9p` paid for the same day: a guard tested only on the\nauthor's idea of the defect passed on the defect itself for ten minutes.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean yx9p"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/conduct/conduct-core/interaction-modality.md#provenance-13",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "The posture, and the condition that revisits it",
      "prov:value": "**The owner chose, 2026-09-20: *\"reminder now, gate later.\"*** The third layer\ndoes **not** block. Asked as: should the `PreToolUse` hook refuse\n`AskUserQuestion` until a validated {@link DecisionRequest} has been rendered?",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-20",
        "owner"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/conduct/conduct-core/interaction-modality.md#provenance-14",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "The posture, and the condition that revisits it",
      "prov:value": "*Superseded, kept as provenance and NOT as the condition:* this said\n**`bean-decision-records`** — beans carrying an `## Options` heading — reading\n**7** on 2026-09-20. **Corrected 2026-09-21 on the owner's ruling** (*\"C —\nrequire `renderDecision`, then revisit\"*, bean `hajp`, [#645](https://github.com/litlfred/folio-assistant/issues/645)).\nThe two metrics count different populations: `bean-decision-records` had grown\n7 → 10 in a day **without anyone adopting anything**, because this store writes\nconsidered-options sections as ordinary practice, while\n`bean-rendered-decision-records` stood at **1** — `hajp` itself. So the old\ncondition would have reached twelve on schedule and delivered **none** of the\nevidence the deferral was granted to buy, which is evidence about whether\n`DecisionRequestSchema` is too narrow, and only a decision that went through it\ncan supply that. `checks.test.ts` states the distinction it missed: *\"an\n`## Options` heading is NOT a rendered decision\"*.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean hajp",
        "#645",
        "https://github.com/litlfred/folio-assistant/issues/645",
        "2026-09-20",
        "2026-09-21",
        "owner"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-20",
        "2026-09-21"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/conduct/conduct-core/interaction-modality.md#provenance-15",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "issue",
      "cat-harness:section": "5. Driving the questions from DMN — one logic, four surfaces",
      "prov:value": "The ask in issue #232 — *force agentic Q&A into guided questions following DMN\nlogic, supporting multiple modalities* — decomposes into two separable things,\nand keeping them separate is the whole design:\n\n**What to ask next** is a decision. It belongs in a DMN table alongside\n`folio-intent.dmn`: inputs are the facts known so far, output is the next\nquestion's id (or `none`, when enough is known). It is authored by whoever owns\nthe process, is reviewable as a table, and is the same for every user.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#232"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
